[{:db/id "q-79699/selection/bebe14febcdd6d74be9ba5d41388eda59ff4220023e47b8d2c7faaaa084d73c1" :answer/id #uuid "0899a31f-35a4-5aa2-8d5b-c6f37a79503e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,+5y=-{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79699/selection/3adf5ec104be14d621527f9602e08fa87c318101c636e3d2214dcd9b433468bf" :answer/id #uuid "57d50d0b-cc09-510e-b593-6ba9ccc3ac07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5xy=-{e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79699/selection/08c71eaadd9998c0994e47d38424578a277fed74226c980cfa787b0d6597e555" :answer/id #uuid "6640317a-3cb8-5bea-83f0-17292460461f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,-5{e}^{x}y=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79699/selection/9c9d2cb0e8b4988cab515b4bd6f6d3147f6f74ff7cf415b40b7230c0ea5a5308" :answer/id #uuid "7f9d4383-844f-5866-ac43-943f2bcff600" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,-5{e}^{x}y=-{e}^{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79699/selection/cc65368782e54501e2663fd03da727426257f5ce24edafb07e5b6c08b77972b1" :answer/id #uuid "d8f8d131-4f75-57e5-948c-c600eda34afd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,+5{e}^{-x}y={e}^{-x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79699/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fb0dacc1-ae55-5143-a1dc-f1223c122e00" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79699/selection/9c9d2cb0e8b4988cab515b4bd6f6d3147f6f74ff7cf415b40b7230c0ea5a5308" :answer-field/choices ["q-79699/selection/bebe14febcdd6d74be9ba5d41388eda59ff4220023e47b8d2c7faaaa084d73c1" "q-79699/selection/3adf5ec104be14d621527f9602e08fa87c318101c636e3d2214dcd9b433468bf" "q-79699/selection/08c71eaadd9998c0994e47d38424578a277fed74226c980cfa787b0d6597e555" "q-79699/selection/9c9d2cb0e8b4988cab515b4bd6f6d3147f6f74ff7cf415b40b7230c0ea5a5308" "q-79699/selection/cc65368782e54501e2663fd03da727426257f5ce24edafb07e5b6c08b77972b1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79699" :question/id #uuid "fd03ddd9-f328-514d-b88e-e72a03336608" :question/math-academy-id "q-79699" :question/problem "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n5{y}^{2}-y{e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=y,\\,y\\ne 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5{y}^{2}-y{e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =y \\\\ -y{e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+5{y}^{2}-y & =0 \\\\ -y({e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y+1) & =0 \\\\ {e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y+1 & =0 \\\\ {e}^{x}({e}^{-x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y+1) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5y{e}^{x}+{e}^{x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,+{{(-5{e}^{x})}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y & ={{-{e}^{x}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-5{e}^{x}y & =-{e}^{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=-5{e}^{x}$ and $Q(x)=-{e}^{x}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79699/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7de671ee-7bba-54ce-bec2-d2d6f5569f4a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79699"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79697/selection/65503d573e6385d2e0b53bfbf2b16f93b0cb2a8581c412bad5ddefe2d7f9d627" :answer/id #uuid "90c54b70-9041-54f5-a98f-4ff97b31361c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-(1+x)y=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79697/selection/7640f220d7365b51e13f9d990c0a9393c96b737dcb931407d77ded4b5e863bc8" :answer/id #uuid "1e48ae81-f48a-5424-ba13-c38e5ba9e359" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy={x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79697/selection/f524ba3fa25d98559e924f903cc54e858b79b4a5056f7bb401833c014583b10f" :answer/id #uuid "89aa8264-9cf4-590d-aac9-fc9a329645ac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+xy=\\frac{1}{x}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79697/selection/0b4f45e8d7c372c8652431197b8407109f55fc00a5fe9a121634609c555ab054" :answer/id #uuid "13b8bb7e-eab1-53c6-8bfc-5c37495edfbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y=-{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79697/selection/4a7fbd9b3514b6635e996effd183ec69bc526d5f592773e488cdf37e122e704a" :answer/id #uuid "a2ff3adc-1903-597f-a75f-bac879c2c06a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy=2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79697/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0fb74fb1-d9f0-5ca2-b97d-af491c2e5634" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79697/selection/7640f220d7365b51e13f9d990c0a9393c96b737dcb931407d77ded4b5e863bc8" :answer-field/choices ["q-79697/selection/65503d573e6385d2e0b53bfbf2b16f93b0cb2a8581c412bad5ddefe2d7f9d627" "q-79697/selection/7640f220d7365b51e13f9d990c0a9393c96b737dcb931407d77ded4b5e863bc8" "q-79697/selection/f524ba3fa25d98559e924f903cc54e858b79b4a5056f7bb401833c014583b10f" "q-79697/selection/0b4f45e8d7c372c8652431197b8407109f55fc00a5fe9a121634609c555ab054" "q-79697/selection/4a7fbd9b3514b6635e996effd183ec69bc526d5f592773e488cdf37e122e704a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79697" :question/id #uuid "796eac59-5d6b-548a-bcd1-69a1ed0d770d" :question/math-academy-id "q-79697" :question/problem "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{x+y}{x}\\,.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A first order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ do not depend on $y.$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}})\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{x+y}{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}(\\frac{x+y}{x}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x(x+y) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={x}^{2}+xy \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,+{{(-x)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y & ={{{x}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy & ={x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=-x$ and $Q(x)={x}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79697/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7de671ee-7bba-54ce-bec2-d2d6f5569f4a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79697"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-16400"] :question/problem "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\n2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=1-4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x & =1-4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ 2\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+4y\\operatorname{sin}⁡x & =1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{{(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y & ={{\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $Q(x)=\\frac{1+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{2}.$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-16396/selection/67bfd02672cdc071f7750a8aadbb5a636f1a7949c80f1e32bdd94caa13f96ddb" :answer/id #uuid "b1ea6302-298f-5852-9619-eee9d8bfc112" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx}-xy=-{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16396/selection/6067d2cb9ab9204642c323579125c19fe1a3eae44538f1fe63eaf154ec5aad94" :answer/id #uuid "37b9f416-0d33-5022-abbb-fb8765da84ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16396/selection/3f7d266858fbdfe386b770654496d9ecd7c2eb4c39a04b4e2778f4caae607a7e" :answer/id #uuid "d3034924-4b7f-5d04-87e2-8d20ab54853a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx}-y=-2x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16396/selection/ad523e2326757a9ae1c10323b98937a37911b4957d3bdfdc2e8e067860e50102" :answer/id #uuid "8d658bfb-edef-57fe-88cb-aa58e6627513" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-{x}^{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16396/selection/345f3f289032707a7047944d85a501e15d06b7c13f892de1579cec4265fa7a3c" :answer/id #uuid "202f2d3b-d782-54e0-9d50-20324448a29f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{1-{x}^{2}}{1+{x}^{2}}y=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-16396/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9b72a3fb-aa2b-5aee-9f67-f74386aea68a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-16396/selection/67bfd02672cdc071f7750a8aadbb5a636f1a7949c80f1e32bdd94caa13f96ddb" :answer-field/choices ["q-16396/selection/67bfd02672cdc071f7750a8aadbb5a636f1a7949c80f1e32bdd94caa13f96ddb" "q-16396/selection/6067d2cb9ab9204642c323579125c19fe1a3eae44538f1fe63eaf154ec5aad94" "q-16396/selection/3f7d266858fbdfe386b770654496d9ecd7c2eb4c39a04b4e2778f4caae607a7e" "q-16396/selection/ad523e2326757a9ae1c10323b98937a37911b4957d3bdfdc2e8e067860e50102" "q-16396/selection/345f3f289032707a7047944d85a501e15d06b7c13f892de1579cec4265fa7a3c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-16396" :question/id #uuid "ec00018b-fca6-56bf-9fcb-4fbfc8967696" :question/math-academy-id "q-16396" :question/problem "Write the following first-order linear ODE in standard form.\n\n$$\ny\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y={y}^{2}x\\,,\\,y\\ne 0\\,.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x)\\,,\n$$\n\nConverting the given equation to standard form, we have\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y & ={y}^{2}x \\\\ y\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}y-{y}^{2}x & =0 \\\\ y(\\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}-yx) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{dy}{dx}+{x}^{2}-yx & =0 \\\\ \\frac{dy}{dx}+\\,{{(-x)}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}y & ={{-{x}^{2}}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)} \\\\ \\frac{dy}{dx}-xy & =-{x}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the equation is written in standard form with $P(x)=-x$ and $Q(x)=-{x}^{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-16396/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7de671ee-7bba-54ce-bec2-d2d6f5569f4a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-16396"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-79753/selection/00252b5e0b4cbb2cb61970b31ecf93fe8516b635c29e79bb3418fb3c3b95ac5a" :answer/id #uuid "363ca8af-ebb3-504a-9fc4-0a004bb2a16d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\sqrt{(xy)}=x+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79753/selection/9fb63e8a5718bf499ad8bd8563d342e60998637c7df4fe7dfadc7a7ca6d5a9b2" :answer/id #uuid "f8f3beed-21e1-543a-af58-76b71d63162f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y={y}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79753/selection/b37b0e9211f999abfa08c64a2e64fc9f40d69317d77ca0f98f66c2a684f3d446" :answer/id #uuid "bd2d2e44-faf2-5c90-bb83-20bbf66c5369" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-xy=\\frac{1}{y-1}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79753/selection/2b7d61eb25f0590d1faf4b245d6d230462e3f713763aed22173386dce78410f1" :answer/id #uuid "91443aa9-d25d-502c-9c6a-6e7b172eaef0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(\\sqrt{x})y=x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79753/selection/d2fd338398cd18df21d85571cdec85f52991eaab7c757aadb016bfc17b726668" :answer/id #uuid "37edf65a-a847-56fb-8404-ae6436165a35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡y" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-79753/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "33b64917-7507-5812-a986-a932f55f8b65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-79753/selection/2b7d61eb25f0590d1faf4b245d6d230462e3f713763aed22173386dce78410f1" :answer-field/choices ["q-79753/selection/00252b5e0b4cbb2cb61970b31ecf93fe8516b635c29e79bb3418fb3c3b95ac5a" "q-79753/selection/9fb63e8a5718bf499ad8bd8563d342e60998637c7df4fe7dfadc7a7ca6d5a9b2" "q-79753/selection/b37b0e9211f999abfa08c64a2e64fc9f40d69317d77ca0f98f66c2a684f3d446" "q-79753/selection/2b7d61eb25f0590d1faf4b245d6d230462e3f713763aed22173386dce78410f1" "q-79753/selection/d2fd338398cd18df21d85571cdec85f52991eaab7c757aadb016bfc17b726668"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-79753" :question/id #uuid "56009a7b-7322-5f2a-a18b-b5d02247377f" :question/math-academy-id "q-79753" :question/problem "Which of the following is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation?" :question/worked-solution "To determine which of the following differential equations is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation, we attempt to write each option in the standard form.\n\nA first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nNote that the option\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+(\\sqrt{x})y=x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x\n$$\n\nis already is written in standard form with  $P(x)=\\sqrt{x}$ and $Q(x)=x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$ Since the equation is written in standard form, we conclude that it is a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations cannot be written in the standard form, and therefore they are not first-order linear ODEs." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79753/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc50a680-dbf8-5d45-a8c3-72c3c15243f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79753"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-103567/selection/4777ffd3191612436a1c59c9bb59b3417140c65bacd0cedde1dfe3bf118bee93" :answer/id #uuid "99662701-943b-5fc4-890b-9bf5468f736b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{y}={x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103567/selection/dbf0265f5194dc5c171bbc12b1ac58dfafcb61e07222fbed554c728909314015" :answer/id #uuid "0cf5376d-0615-5f31-b249-60808562f1c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-y{e}^{2x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103567/selection/4f9a5aad0adf821eb3ec7c12dc42efe15793a95b140e25e14f86bc779039d17c" :answer/id #uuid "9d5448e4-1987-57d3-9205-e1a9b2118b71" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103567/selection/03f8514da25a9f98ded39382901e473ed2173b3df8528adf4297485098da4002" :answer/id #uuid "5e1a28a4-3e38-5072-b4a2-dc4c03f25705" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{2x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103567/selection/18066732cd9ddfcaf3676c95f0cd6c78ff96754a3404b40890e832fe4afff084" :answer/id #uuid "eb8264bc-dc17-5abc-aa89-7ad75fe0b602" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+x{e}^{2x}y=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{y}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-103567/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "835b469b-e1d0-52d7-9659-86f89681c74e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-103567/selection/03f8514da25a9f98ded39382901e473ed2173b3df8528adf4297485098da4002" :answer-field/choices ["q-103567/selection/4777ffd3191612436a1c59c9bb59b3417140c65bacd0cedde1dfe3bf118bee93" "q-103567/selection/dbf0265f5194dc5c171bbc12b1ac58dfafcb61e07222fbed554c728909314015" "q-103567/selection/4f9a5aad0adf821eb3ec7c12dc42efe15793a95b140e25e14f86bc779039d17c" "q-103567/selection/03f8514da25a9f98ded39382901e473ed2173b3df8528adf4297485098da4002" "q-103567/selection/18066732cd9ddfcaf3676c95f0cd6c78ff96754a3404b40890e832fe4afff084"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-103567" :question/id #uuid "420cf089-e2ca-55d0-b4d5-3e91f54aadf7" :question/math-academy-id "q-103567" :question/problem "Which of the following is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation?" :question/worked-solution "To determine which of the following differential equations is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation, we attempt to write each option in the standard form.\n\nA first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nLet's attempt to write $\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{2x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{y}$ in the standard form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{2x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{2x}y & =y\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-x{e}^{2x}y & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is in standard form with  $P(x)=-x{e}^{2x}$ and $Q(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.$ Since the equation is written in standard form, we conclude that it is a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations cannot be written in the standard form, and therefore they are not first-order linear ODEs." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-103567/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bc50a680-dbf8-5d45-a8c3-72c3c15243f6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-103567"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8349"] :question/worked-solution "To determine which of the following differential equations is a first-order linear ordinary differential equation, we attempt to write each option in the standard form.\n\nA first-order linear ODE is in standard form if it is written as\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x).\n$$\n\nNote that the option\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+2xy=6{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nis already is written in standard form with  $P(x)=2x$ and $Q(x)=6{x}^{2}.$ Since the equation is written in standard form, we conclude that it is a first-order linear ODE.\n\nAll of the other equations cannot be written in the standard form, and therefore they are not first-order linear ODEs." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-331727/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ec0f3bd0-c71a-50d3-9758-0c003ccdb155" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331727/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "cef4c664-c04b-5a11-9961-c6998c3a2a49" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331727/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "4287d5b0-0643-57c7-87c5-fe38b332f22f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331727/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "c4ac63c7-9e16-5896-9b00-031871696efb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331727/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "5cfe0a84-8ced-5f34-bf7b-0743a8aa0a3d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331727/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c1850d7-1a6d-59a6-b56e-3444e0564b36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-331727/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-331727/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-331727/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-331727/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-331727/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-331727/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331727" :question/id #uuid "4fc87950-d591-5333-8bfb-dd5aa9b78b7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-331727" :question/problem "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are homogeneous?\n\n- ${y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=-3y$\n- ${y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=x$\n- ${y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=0$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each equation in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=-3y.\n$$\n\nWe move the term involving $y$ to the left side so that all $y$-terms are together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y & =-3y \\\\ {y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y+3y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+({x}^{2}+3)y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$  Therefore, this equation *is* homogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=x.\n$$\n\nNotice that this is written in the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)$ where $Q(x)=x$ is not identically zero. Therefore, this equation is inhomogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+{x}^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is already zero, so the equation directly matches the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331727/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739a8f10-413a-5a1d-a47e-4afd0b14eb44"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331727"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331724/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "70d24f13-cf29-5e13-becd-f507c2aada4f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331724/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "99b06fcb-4874-596f-8545-e6dd462e09f4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331724/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "4a03aed5-df62-5eb0-b0a0-7758e463580e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331724/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "6a762ec9-6315-51df-895e-77ae8fba1514" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331724/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "34d35e32-b10c-534a-be15-2cf90467de39" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331724/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "24fc08da-8471-5a09-8390-f7258f4ee14e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-331724/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-331724/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-331724/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-331724/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-331724/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-331724/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331724" :question/id #uuid "47c2e09f-c0f7-56b8-b5a4-7e98b72cdc6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-331724" :question/problem "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are homogeneous?\n\n- ${y}^{′}+2{x}^{3}y={x}^{2}$\n- ${y}^{′}+2{x}^{3}y=-3y$\n- ${y}^{′}+2{x}^{3}y=0$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each equation in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+2{x}^{3}y={x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that this is written in the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)$ where $Q(x)={x}^{2}$ is not identically zero. Therefore, this equation is inhomogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+2{x}^{3}y=-3y.\n$$\n\nWe move the term involving $y$ to the left side so that all $y$-terms are together:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}+2{x}^{3}y & =-3y \\\\ {y}^{′}+2{x}^{3}y+3y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}+(2{x}^{3}+3)y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$  Therefore, this equation *is* homogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+2{x}^{3}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is already zero, so the equation directly matches the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-331724/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739a8f10-413a-5a1d-a47e-4afd0b14eb44"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331724"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-331739/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "db5ce2a9-0906-5a68-9103-2db968c517f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331739/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "0abab218-2c14-51f4-8d8e-30f77e1e56ba" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331739/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" :answer/id #uuid "1a40f4f8-d24a-51ed-95ee-387b8987a252" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331739/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "cf481d94-42ca-53d5-8b86-ee0372b2a33f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331739/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "f5129718-2a0e-538f-aaa7-e78f1c18d852" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-331739/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "05abac35-1617-51ec-bfb5-85e6776904f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-331739/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-331739/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-331739/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-331739/selection/1e5815fe88f764dcffb6e1d4884bd91ce2c23cb2e4c57c2f2f99b70378aa1f23" "q-331739/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-331739/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-331739" :question/id #uuid "8ae95313-5ad6-52d8-8e38-94f4839c14a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-331739" :question/problem "Which of the following first-order linear differential equations are inhomogeneous?\n\n- ${y}^{′}-{x}^{2}y={x}^{3}$\n- ${y}^{′}-{x}^{2}y=y$\n- ${y}^{′}-{x}^{2}y=0$" :question/worked-solution "A first-order linear differential equation is homogeneous if it can be written in the form\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.\n$$\n\nA first-order linear differential equation is inhomogeneous if it is not homogeneous, i.e., if it can be written as\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwhere $Q$ is not identical to zero.\n\nTo determine which equations are inhomogeneous, we examine each one in turn.\n\n- First, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-{x}^{2}y={x}^{3}.\n$$\n\nNotice that this is written in the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=Q(x)$ where $Q(x)={x}^{3}$ is not identically zero. Therefore, this equation is inhomogeneous.\n\n- Next, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-{x}^{2}y=y.\n$$\n\nWe collect the $y$-terms on the left side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}-{x}^{2}y & =y \\\\ {y}^{′}-{x}^{2}y-y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{′}-({x}^{2}+1)y & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis matches the homogeneous form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$  Therefore, this equation *is* homogeneous.\n\n- Finally, we consider the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}-{x}^{2}y=0.\n$$\n\nThe right-hand side is already zero, so the equation directly matches the form ${y}^{′}+P(x)y=0.$ Therefore, this equation is homogeneous.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-331739/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "739a8f10-413a-5a1d-a47e-4afd0b14eb44"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-331739"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
